<title>GREECE: CITIBANK, ATHENS TO CUT MORTGAGE RATE BY 50 BPS.</title>
<headline>CITIBANK, ATHENS TO CUT MORTGAGE RATE BY 50 BPS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will cut its base mortgage</p>
<p>rate by 50 basis points but leave all other base loan rates</p>
<p>unchanged effective on Tuesday, it said.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following lending rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 16.25 percent</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate at 17.00 percent</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 16.50 percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate at 15.50 from 16 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans at 23 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 21 percent</p>
<p>** Auto loans through representative at 18.75 percent</p>
<p>** Branch auto loans at 19.75 percent</p>
<p>** Home improvement loans at 19.75 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Base rates on working capital loans in foreign currency for</p>
<p>the coming week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  8.00 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.80 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  3.12 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.65 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.73 percent</p>
<p>    Pounds Sterling:  8.75 percent</p>
<p>    French francs  :  5.83 percent</p>
<p>    Swiss francs   :  4.18 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
